{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' 'test/Seven Rivers/Seven Rivers.RPP'; find 'test/Seven Rivers' -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort; git show --format=fuller --no-patch 5893c2a; gh issue view 2 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json title,body,comments,labels\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Implement **phase 0** of vgt — the REAPER-plumbing foundation defined in [`docs/GOAL.md`](docs/GOAL.md). This is the first implementation task; it sets up the repo skeleton and the core non-destructive project-manipulation path. The full analysis pipeline in `docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md` is **out of scope**.\\n\\n## Scope (from docs/GOAL.md)\\n\\n- **Locate a REAPER project** — accept a project path as input.\\n- **Default to the current project** — when no path is given and a `.RPP` exists in the working directory, use it.\\n- **Open and read relevant info** — parse the project and read at least: sample rate, tempo/time-signature, and the existing track list (names + GUIDs), so vgt can tell which tracks it already manages.\\n- **Store vgt settings** — a single `vgt.json` sidecar next to the `.RPP` (schema version, GUIDs of vgt-created tracks, config).\\n- **Prepare a `[vgt]`-managed area** — a track folder + `[vgt]` name prefix on everything vgt creates.\\n- **Create one track** in that area that initially mirrors the original song.\\n\\n## Hard requirements\\n\\n- **Non-destructive:** never overwrite, rename, or delete any track/object vgt did not create. Only `[vgt]`-prefixed objects are ever touched; re-apply removes only its own `[vgt]` objects before recreating them.\\n- **Idempotent:** running the same command twice produces the same result — no duplicate tracks/folders/settings.\\n- **Respect REAPER settings:** honor the project's existing sample rate, tempo, etc.\\n- **Prefer the REAPER API** (ReaScript action) over editing `.RPP` text, so changes appear live in the user's open project. Where a piece isn't yet feasible in-app, note it explicitly rather than silently text-editing.\\n- **CLI-initiated:** build the CLI now (intended to be called from a ReaScript action later).\\n- **Documented:** how vgt works and how to run it.\\n\\n## Environment / test\\n\\n- REAPER may be assumed installed (7.x, `/Applications/REAPER.app` on macOS) — see `docs/AGENTS.md`.\\n- A real fixture project lives at **`test/Seven Rivers/`** (read-mostly; work against a copy, never commit vgt's mutations into `test/`).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `vgt` CLI runs; with no arg it finds the `.RPP` in the working dir, with an arg it opens the given project.\\n- [ ] Reads and reports sample rate, tempo/time-sig, and track list from `test/Seven Rivers/Seven Rivers.RPP`.\\n- [ ] Creates/updates a `vgt.json` sidecar next to the project.\\n- [ ] Creates a `[vgt]` folder + one mirror track; re-running is idempotent (no duplicates) and leaves the original 4 tracks untouched.\\n- [ ] Basic docs (README/usage) present.\\n\\nBreak out sub-issues if any part must land first; otherwise implement as one PR-sized unit.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnfA\",\"name\":\"status:working\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEpBQ\",\"name\":\"priority:high\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"d93f0b\"}],\"title\":\"Phase 0: REAPER project plumbing (locate, read, vgt-managed area, mirror track)\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
